# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT USE GIT LFS.
#
# The Figma Make scaffold shipped a generated .gitattributes that routed every
# *.png / *.webp / *.mp4 / *.woff2 through `filter=lfs`. That is a hard
# deployment blocker on Vercel: Vercel clones the repo WITHOUT fetching LFS
# objects, so the build would see ~130-byte pointer files where the plates and
# the Lamp Lighting video should be. Vite would happily hash and emit those
# pointers as "images", and every photograph on the deployed site would be
# broken — with a green build log.
#
# The shipped assets total ~3.2MB (see src/imports/), which plain Git carries
# without complaint. Do not reintroduce LFS filters here unless Vercel's LFS
# checkout is configured first.

# Normalise text files to LF in the repo, checkout native on Windows.
* text=auto

# Anything Git might otherwise line-ending-mangle or try to diff. `binary` is
# shorthand for `-diff -merge -text`.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.avif   binary
*.svg    text eol=lf
*.mp4    binary
*.webm   binary
*.mov    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary

# Keep shell scripts LF so the Figma Make helpers in .figma/make stay runnable.
*.sh     text eol=lf
